===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q189233}}An [[impressive]] [[seat]] [[use]]d by a [[monarch]], [[often]] on a [[raised]] [[dais]] in a [[throne room]] and [[reserve]]d for [[formal]] [[occasion]]s.
#: {{ux|en|He approached the '''throne''' reverently.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Revelation|7|9|12|passage=9 After this I beheld, and lo, a great multitude, which no man could nūber, of all nations, and kindreds, and people, & tongues, stood before the '''throne''', & before the Lamb, clothed with white robes, and palmes in their hands:<br>10 And cryed with a loude voice, saying, Saluation to our God, which sitteth vpon the '''Throne''', and vnto the Lambe.<br>11 And all the Angels stood round about the '''Throne''', and about the Elders, and the foure beasts, and fell before the '''throne''' on their faces, and worshipped God,<br>12 Saying, Amen: Blessing, and glorie, and wisedome, and thankesgiuing, and honour, & power, and might be vnto our God for euer & euer, Amen.}}
# {{label|en|figuratively}} [[leadership|Leadership]], ''[[particularly]]'' the [[position]] of a [[monarch]].
#: ''[[w:Queen Victoria|Queen Victoria]] sat upon the '''throne''' of England for 63 years.''
#: {{ux|en|The prince's newborn baby is fifth in line to the '''throne'''.}}
#* '''1611''', [[w:Bible|Bible]] ([[w:King James Version|KJV]]), [[w:Genesis|Genesis]], [http://www.kingjamesbibleonline.org/1611_Genesis-Chapter-41/#40 41:40]:
#*: [[thou|Thou]] [[shall|shalt]] be [[over|ouer]] my house, and according [[unto|vnto]] [[thy]] word shall all my people be ruled: only in the '''throne''' will I be greater [[than|then]] [[thou]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023 December 27|author=Stephen Roberts|title=Bradshaw's Britain: the way to Weymouth|journal=RAIL|issue=999|page=52|text=Stephen reigned from 1135-1154, that nasty period of our history dubbed 'The Anarchy', when forces loyal to Stephen contested the '''throne''' with those of Henry I's daughter Matilda, who by rights should have been queen. Stephen, her cousin, plonked his own posterior on the '''throne'''.}}
# The seat of a [[bishop]] in the cathedral-church of his [[diocese]]; also, the seat of a [[pope]].
#: {{syn|en|cathedra}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1936|author=Rollo Ahmed|title=The Black Art|publisher=Long|location=London|page=105|passage=Pope Joan, who once occupied the '''throne''' of the Vatican, was reputed to be the blackest sorcerer of them all.}}
# {{label|en|euphemism}} A [[toilet]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1991|author=Stephen King|title=Needful Things
|passage="If she has intestinal flu, you probably called while she was on the '''throne''' and she didn't want to admit it," Alan said dryly.}}
# {{lb|en|music}} A [[kind]] of [[stool]] [[use]]d by [[drummer]]s.
# {{lb|en|Christianity}} A member of an [[order]] of [[angel]]s [[rank]]ed above [[dominion]]s and below [[cherub]]im.
#* '''1611''', [[w:Bible|Bible]] ([[w:King James Version|KJV]]), [[w:Colossians|Epistle of Paul to the Colossians]], [http://www.kingjamesbibleonline.org/1611_Colossians-Chapter-1/#16 1:16]:
#*: For by him were all things created that are in [[heaven|heauen]], and that are in earth, visible and [[invisible|inuisible]], whether they be '''thrones''', or dominions, or principalities, or powers: all things were created by him, and for him.

